In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires the Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam established by 3( 1); "bank" means{a} in relation to Brunei Darussalam, a bank licensed under sections 4 or 23 of the Banking Order, 2006 (S 45/06), an international bank licensed section 7 of the International Banking Order, 2000 {S 53/00) and an bank licensed under sections 4 or 23 of the Islamic Banking Order, 2008 (S 96/08); {b) in relation to any country, territory or place outside Brunei Darussalam, a person lawfully carrying on therein business corresponding in part or in substance to "banking business" as defined in section 2(1) of the Banking Order, 2006 (S 45/06) or in section 2(1) of the International Order, 2000 {S 53/00); and includes Islamic banking business as defined in section 2(1) of the Islamic Banking Order, 2008 (S 96/08); means the board of directors of the Authority established by means a director of the board appointed under section 12(1); "financial institution" means

(a) any insurer registered under the Insurance Order, 2006 (S 48/06) or the Takaful Order, 2008 (S 100/08) or any person licensed the International Insurance and Takaful Order, 2002 (S 43/02); {b} any finance company licensed under the Finance Companies 89);

(c) any person licensed under the Registered Agents and Trustees Licensing Order, 2000 (S 54/00), the Mutual Funds Order, 2001 (S 18/01), the Securities Order, 2001 (S 31/01) or the International Insurance and Takaful Order, 2002 (S 43/02); {d} any person licensed to carry on any money-changing business or remittance business under the Money-Changing and Remittance Businesses Act (Chapter 174);

(e) such other person licensed, approved or regulated by the under any written law; "managing director" means the director appointed to be the managing under section 13( 1); means the Minister of Finance; means the reserve fund to be established under {a}.

AND CAPITAL OF AUTHORITY of Authority.

( 1) The principal objects of the Authority shall be

(a) to achieve and maintain domestic price stability;

(b) to ensure the stability of the financial system, in particular by formulating financial regulation and prudential standards;

(c) to assist in the establishment and functioning of efficient payment and to oversee them; and

(d) to foster and develop a sound and progressive financial services sector. (21 prejudice to the above-mentioned principal objects, the shall support the general economic policies of the Government to the that it considers to be appropriate. etc. of Authority.

(1) The net profits or losses determined by the Authority shall be in conformity with the accounting standards adopted by the Authority.

(2) The earnings available for distribution under section 9 shall be {a) where profits include realised and unrealised foreign currency by deducting the amount of such gains from the net profits and adding the amount to the currency valuation reserve fund; {b) where profits include realised and unrealised foreign currency valuation losses, by adding back such losses to the net profits and deducting the amount from the currency valuation reserve fund to the extent that there are credit funds available in the currency valuation reserve fund to cover such losses;

(c) where profits include market unrealised valuation gains, by the amount of such gains from the net profits and adding the to the market valuation reserve fund;

(d) where profits include market unrealised valuation losses, by adding back such losses to the net profit and deducting such losses from the market reserve fund to the extent that there are credit funds available in the market valuation reserve fund to cover such losses. Allocation of distributable earnings.

Where in the audited annual financial statements of the Authority, the value of its assets falls below the sum of its monetary liabilities and its unimpaired capital, then - (a} the Authority, with the advice of the external auditor of the shall assess the situation and prepare a report on the causes and of the shortfall and assess the situation within a period of no more than 30 days;

(b) if the Authority approves such report, the Authority shall request the Government for a capital contribution to be made by the Government to the net capital position to the original amount of the issued capital; and {c) upon receipt of the request referred in paragraph {b), the shall, within a period of not more than 30 days, transfer to the Authority the necessary amount in currency or in negotiable securities with a maturity issued at market rates prevailing in Brunei Darussalam as its capital contribution.

OF AUTHORITY of directors.

The duties of the Head of Internal Audit shall include - {a} the review and recommendation to the Authority and the Audit Committee of procedures and practices for proper risk and management and and the supervision of their implementation on a continuing basis;

(b) the performance of periodic audits of the administration and operations of the Authority to ensure proper observance of laws applicable to and of decisions of the Authority;

(c) the review of the periodic financial statements referred to in and related documents of the Authority;

(d) the preparation and delivery to the Authority, whenever considered appropriate by the managing director, the Authority or the Audit Committee and at least once every quarter, of reports and recommendations regarding the financial statements and records, the budgetary and accounting the risk management and other controls within the Authority, and its cost effectiveness at which the Authority operates, and any other matter within its competence and area of responsibility on which a may be requested by the managing director, the Authority or the Audit

(e) any other assignments that may be given by the Authority or the Committee, provided that any such assignment does not disrupt its and

(f) liaising with the external auditors of the Authority. of employees.

No action, suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against(a) the Authority;

(b) any director or employee of the Authority; (cJ any public officer; {d) any person who is on secondment or attachment to the Authority; or (eJ any person appointed, approved or directed to exercise the of the Authority or to assist the Authority in the exercise of its under this Order or under any other written law, for anything done !including any statement made) or omitted to be done in good the course of or in connection with -

(i) the exercise or purported exercise of any power under this or that other written law;

(ii) the performance or purported performance of any function or duty under this Order or that other written law; or

(iii) the compliance or purported compliance with this Order or that other written law. Remuneration not to be related to profits.

(1) In implementing its objects, the Authority may, exercise and discharge the following functions, powers and duties {a} act as the central bank of Brunei Darussalam, including the conduct of monetary policy, the issuance of the currency of Brunei Darussalam, the payment systems and serving as banker to and financial agent of the Government; {b) manage the exchange rate regulation regime, in particular by entering into foreign exchange arrangements, without prejudice to the principal objects of the Authority and after consultation with the {c) determine, where applicable, the conditions of employment of the agents, including receivers of banks and financial institutions, and correspondents; {d} determine the conditions of employment of the staff of the including their appointment, promotion, conduct and discipline and to determine the conditions applicable to the advisers of the Authority; {e) determine denominations and design of banknotes, coins and their and handling;

(f) hold, manage, use and dispose of the foreign reserves of the {g) develop and manage an inter-bank funds system and establish the requirements for its participants;

(h) establish principles and procedures for financial accounting and of banks and financial institutions in Brunei Darussalam and of banks and financial institutions of foreign countries or territories operating in Brunei Darussalam; (i} form or participate in the formation of any body corporate or in any venture as a shareholder or partner or in any other capacity, for that are necessary or expedient for the purpose of discharging its functions or achieving its objects; (j} carry out any ancillary activities incidental to the exercise of its under this Order or any other written law; and (k} exercise and discharge such other functions, powers and duties by this Order or any other written law.

(2) The Authority shall carry out activities necessary for the implementation of the functions specified in subsection ( 1) and for the development and maintenance of the infrastructure needed for their implementation. of accounts.
